hc","d5"],["at","\nWest leads the @D5 against your contract of Four Spades."],["pg",""],["lc","d5"],["pc","d5"],["hs","sc"],["nt","\nYou can afford three losers. It looks like you have four losers: three Clubs "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["hs","sd"],["at","and a Diamond. There is nowhere to discard any of your losers and you can't trump any in the dummy. Is there any hope?"],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["hc","dk"],["nt","\nYou are missing the @DK, "],["pg",""],["lc","dk"],["hc","dq"],["at","but you have the @DQ in your hand. West's Diamond lead gives you some chance because you play last to the trick. "],["pg",""],["lc","dq"],["hc","da"],["at","If you take dummy's @DA, "],["pg",""],["lc","da"],["pc","da"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hc","dq"],["at","your @DQ will be singleton "],["pg",""],["lc","dq"],["hc","dk"],["at","and you will eventually lose it to the opponents' @DK. "],["pg",""],["lc","dk"],["up","3"],["hs","nd"],["nt","\nBut what if you play a small card from dummy on the first trick, "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["pc","d"],["hc","dq"],["at","hoping to win your @DQ? "],["pg",""],["lc","dq"],["hc","dk"],["at","If East doesn't have the @DK, "],["pg",""],["lc","dk"],["hs","ed"],["at","as on the above layout, "],["pg",""],["ls","ed"],["pc","dj"],["hc","dq"],["at","your @DQ will win the trick "],["pg",""],["lc","dq"],["pc","dq"],["pg",""],["hs","sd"],["at","and you will no longer have a Diamond loser."],["pg",""],["up","3"],["hs","wd"],["ls","sd"],["nt","\nWest's choice of opening lead was unfortunate for the defenders, but you had to understand the positional value of playing last to a trick to take advantage of it."],["",""]]}}